nt/self-hosted/networking-2","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking#do-you-need-gatewayaddresses","content":"Do you need `gateway.addresses`?"},"238":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking-3","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking#recommended-single-node-design","content":"Recommended single-node design"},"239":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking-4","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking#k3s","content":"K3s"},"240":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking-5","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking#bare-metal-with-metallb-or-kube-vip","content":"Bare metal with MetalLB or kube-vip"},"241":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking-6","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking#external-reverse-proxy-nat-or-vpn","content":"External reverse proxy, NAT or VPN"},"242":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking-7","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking#what-if-you-need-three-gateways","content":"What if you need three Gateways?"},"243":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking-8","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking#decision-guide","content":"Decision guide"},"244":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking-9","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking#verify-the-traffic-path","content":"Verify the traffic path"},"245":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking-10","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking#expose-the-lamassu-gateway","content":"The Lamassu chart creates one shared Gateway with HTTP and HTTPS listeners. Envoy Gateway normally creates a dedicated proxy deployment and a `LoadBalancer` Service for it."},"246":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking-11","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking#expose-the-lamassu-gateway","content":"External reachability is the result of the whole path. A `Gateway` resource alone does not configure your router, firewall, DNS, cloud load balancer or upstream NAT."},"247":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking-12","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking#do-you-need-gatewayaddresses","content":"Usually, no. If you omit it, the Gateway controller and the cluster load-balancer implementation can assign an address and report it in `Gateway.status.addresses` and the generated Service status."},"248":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking-13","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking#do-you-need-gatewayaddresses","content":"Set it only when:"},"249":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking-14","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking#do-you-need-gatewayaddresses","content":"your cloud or bare-metal load balancer supports requesting a specific address"},"250":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking-15","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking#do-you-need-gatewayaddresses","content":"that address is allocated to this Gateway"},"251":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking-16","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking#do-you-need-gatewayaddresses","content":"the surrounding network already routes traffic for it to the cluster"},"252":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking-17","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking#do-you-need-gatewayaddresses","content":"This requests `192.168.1.50`; it does not claim the IP on your LAN or make it reachable."},"253":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking-18","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking#do-you-need-gatewayaddresses","content":"Keep these two settings separate:"},"254":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking-19","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking#do-you-need-gatewayaddresses","content":"`gateway.addresses` requests an address for the Gateway."},"255":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking-20","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking#do-you-need-gatewayaddresses","content":"`tls.certManagerOptions.certSpec.addresses` adds IP subject alternative names to the TLS certificate."},"256":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking-21","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking#do-you-need-gatewayaddresses","content":"If users connect by DNS name, put that name in `tls.certManagerOptions.certSpec.hostnames`. Do not copy an upstream proxy's public IP into `gateway.addresses`."},"257":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking-22","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking#recommended-single-node-design","content":"For a small VM running K3s or MicroK8s, use one external Lamassu Gateway and route every Lamassu endpoint through it:"},"258":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking-23","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking#recommended-single-node-design","content":"This design uses one IP, one TLS entry point and one pair of ports. The chart already creates the required routes."},"259":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking-24","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking#k3s","content":"K3s ServiceLB implements each `LoadBalancer` Service with pods that reserve the Service ports on the node. On a single node, only one Service can therefore own port 80 and one can own port 443. The default K3s Traefik Service may already hold both ports."},"260":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking-25","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking#k3s","content":"For the recommended design:"},"261":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking-26","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking#k3s","content":"Use only one externally exposed Lamassu Gateway."},"262":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking-27","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking#k3s","content":"Ensure ports 80 and 443 are free. Disable or reconfigure Traefik if it is not part of your traffic path."},"263":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking-28","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking#k3s","content":"Allow those ports through the VM firewall and any upstream security group."},"264":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking-29","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking#k3s","content":"Point DNS at the VM's reachable address."},"265":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking-30","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking#k3s","content":"See the K3s ServiceLB documentation for its host-port behavior and how to replace it with another load-balancer implementation."},"266":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking-31","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking#bare-metal-with-metallb-or-kube-vip","content":"Allocate a VIP from an address pool reachable on your LAN. You may request that VIP with `gateway.addresses` if the selected implementation supports it. Confirm the assigned address in status rather than assuming the request succeeded."},"267":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking-32","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking#external-reverse-proxy-nat-or-vpn","content":"An external public address can forward TCP 80 and 443 to the VM or to a Kubernetes-side VIP:"},"268":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking-33","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking#external-reverse-proxy-nat-or-vpn","content":"The public IP belongs to the external device. Leave `gateway.addresses` unset or set it to the actual Kubernetes-side address, never to an address that the cluster cannot bind."},"269":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking-34","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking#what-if-you-need-three-gateways","content":"First decide whether you need three independent data planes or only three hostnames."},"270":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking-35","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking#what-if-you-need-three-gateways","content":"Requirement"},"271":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking-36","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking#what-if-you-need-three-gateways","content":"Recommended design"},"272":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking-37","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking#what-if-you-need-three-gateways","content":"Consequence"},"273":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking-38","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking#what-if-you-need-three-gateways","content":"Several Lamassu URLs or services"},"274":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking-39","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking#what-if-you-need-three-gateways","content":"One Gateway with multiple routes"},"275":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking-40","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking#what-if-you-need-three-gateways","content":"One IP and one proxy fleet; this is the chart default"},"276":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking-41","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking#what-if-you-need-three-gateways","content":"Independent Gateways and separate external IPs"},"277":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking-42","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking#what-if-you-need-three-gateways","content":"One VIP per Gateway"},"278":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking-43","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking#what-if-you-need-three-gateways","content":"All Gateways can use 80/443; requires a load balancer with an address pool"},"279":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking-44","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking#what-if-you-need-three-gateways","content":"Independent Gateways on one node and one IP"},"280":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking-45","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking#what-if-you-need-three-gateways","content":"Use different external ports"},"281":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking-46","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking#what-if-you-need-three-gateways","content":"Clients must include non-standard ports"},"282":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking-47","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking#what-if-you-need-three-gateways","content":"Separate TLS/mTLS termination behind one IP"},"283":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking-48","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking#what-if-you-need-three-gateways","content":"Front-door SNI routing to internal Gateways"},"284":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking-49","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking#what-if-you-need-three-gateways","content":"Advanced design; the front door uses TLS passthrough and each internal Gateway terminates its own TLS"},"285":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking-50","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking#what-if-you-need-three-gateways","content":"Separate Gateway resources but shared proxy infrastructure"},"286":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking-51","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking#what-if-you-need-three-gateways","content":"Envoy merged-Gateway mode"},"287":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking-52","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking#what-if-you-need-three-gateways","content":"Logical separation only; listeners must have unique port, protocol and hostname tuples"},"288":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking-53","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-38/deployment/self-hosted/networking#what-if-you-need-three-gateways","content":"Three independent `LoadBalancer` Services cannot all reserve the same node ports 80 and 443 through K3s ServiceLB. Use one shared Gateway, allocate distinct VIPs with another load-balancer implementation, or use different port